# Performance Rules

## Responsibilities

- Maintain fast page loads and interactions for daily lawyer workflows
- Optimize database queries, bundle size, and rendering strategy
- Monitor Core Web Vitals (LCP <2.5s, INP <200ms, CLS <0.1)

## Best Practices

- **Server Components** for static/slow-changing content
- **React Query** staleTime: 30s lists, 5min reference data
- **Pagination** default 25, max 100 per request
- **Image optimization** via next/image with proper sizes
- **Font optimization** via next/font (Geist/Inter)
- **Bundle analysis** monthly via `@next/bundle-analyzer`
- **Database**: select specific fields, avoid N+1, use indexes

## Coding Standards

```typescript
// Parallel data fetching in Server Component
const [cases, stats] = await Promise.all([
  caseRepository.list(orgId, filters),
  dashboardRepository.getStats(orgId),
]);

// React Query prefetch on hover
const prefetchCase = (id: string) => {
  queryClient.prefetchQuery({ queryKey: ['case', id], queryFn: () => getCase(id) });
};
```

## Folder Structure

```
src/lib/cache/          # Cache tag constants, revalidation helpers
src/components/feedback/ # Skeleton components matching layouts
```

## Naming Convention

- Cache tags: `{entity}` or `{entity}:{id}` → `cases`, `case:clxyz`
- Dynamic import files: `[feature]-chart.tsx` lazy loaded

## Performance Rules (Detailed)

| Area | Rule |
|------|------|
| Lists | Virtualize >100 rows |
| Search | Debounce 300ms, min 2 chars |
| Files | Presigned URLs, CDN for documents |
| Charts | Dynamic import, render on tab visible |
| Animations | 60fps, transform/opacity only |
| DB | Query <50ms p95 for list endpoints |
| Bundle | Client JS <200KB initial per route |

## Security Rules

- Rate limit expensive endpoints (search, export)
- Paginate exports — never load full table to memory

## Examples

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — Dynamic import heavy component
const RevenueChart = dynamic(() => import('./revenue-chart'), {
  loading: () => <ChartSkeleton />,
  ssr: false,
});

// ✅ GOOD — Select only needed fields
prisma.case.findMany({
  select: { id: true, title: true, status: true, client: { select: { name: true } } },
});
```

## Things to Avoid

- Fetching entire object graphs with deep includes
- Client-side filtering of large datasets fetched once
- Unoptimized images (raw `<img>` tags)
- Synchronous file operations on request path
- Missing Suspense boundaries causing full-page blocking

## Checklist Before Finishing Any Task

- [ ] List views paginated
- [ ] Skeleton loaders prevent CLS
- [ ] No N+1 query patterns introduced
- [ ] Heavy components lazy-loaded
- [ ] Images use next/image
- [ ] Revalidation strategy defined for cached data
